# What EAS Build uploads from this repo.
#
# When this file exists EAS reads it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so every rule that
# keeps a secret out of git has to be repeated here or the secret goes up with
# the archive. The secrets block below is copied from .gitignore verbatim; keep
# the two in step.
#
# The only build that runs from this repo is the apps/mobile client. It needs
# apps/mobile, packages/* (where its workspace:* deps live) and the root manifests
# so pnpm can resolve every importer in the lockfile. Everything heavy in the
# other workspaces is dead weight: the first upload was 296 MB and failed
# mid-transfer, almost all of it apps/web/.next and apps/web/public.

# ── Secrets (verbatim from .gitignore) ───────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Build output and caches (from .gitignore) ────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
apps/*/dist/
apps/*/.next/
apps/*/.next-prod/
apps/*/.next-build/
apps/*/.turbo/
apps/*/.expo/
apps/*/out/
apps/*/build/
server/*/dist/
server/*/.turbo/
server/*/build/
tools/*/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
*.log

# ── Not needed for a mobile build ────────────────────────────────────────────
# 148 MB of web assets. Keep the web workspace's package.json so the lockfile
# importer still resolves; drop only the payload.
apps/web/public/

# ── Editor, OS, AI context ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
